GPU CFD Solver

3D incompressible/compressible CFD solver running entirely on GPU using OpenGL shader compute pipelines on a 192³ grid.

Includes:

Real-time volumetric raymarching visualizer
Dark-themed GUI launcher
NACA airfoil generation
CAD mesh import
Multigrid pressure solving
Aerodynamic force analysis
Quick Start
# Activate environment
source venv/bin/activate

# Launch GUI
__NV_PRIME_RENDER_OFFLOAD=1 \
__GLX_VENDOR_LIBRARY_NAME=nvidia \
python launcher.py
Launcher Tabs
1. Object Selection

Choose simulation geometry:

NACA 4-digit airfoils
NACA 5-digit airfoils
NACA 6-series airfoils
Cylinder
Sphere
Custom .stl mesh import

Live airfoil preview included.

2. Emitters

Configure dye injection regions.

Includes optional 3D viewport for visual emitter placement.

3. Fluid & Simulation Settings
Setting	Purpose
Velocity	Freestream velocity
Reynolds Number	Automatic viscosity control
Viscosity	Manual viscosity override
Steps	Total simulation steps
Save Every	Frame save interval
Solver	RBGS or Multigrid V-cycle
Mode	Incompressible / Compressible
Mach	Compressible flow Mach number
Output Directory	Saved simulation frames
4. Run

The launcher:

Starts the simulation
Opens the live raymarch visualizer
Streams simulation frames in real time
Displays progress/log output
Visualizer Controls
Key	Action
Left Drag	Orbit camera
Scroll	Zoom
Space	Pause/Resume
Arrow Keys	Step frames
V	Change visualization mode
ESC	Exit
CLI Example
__NV_PRIME_RENDER_OFFLOAD=1 \
__GLX_VENDOR_LIBRARY_NAME=nvidia \
python simulate_cfd.py \
  --obstacle wing \
  --aoa 5 \
  --wind 2.0 \
  --steps 500 \
  --save-every 2 \
  --no-forces

Launch visualizer:

python visualize_cfd.py
GPU Requirement

Requires:

NVIDIA GPU recommended
OpenGL 3.3+ support

The __NV_PRIME_RENDER_OFFLOAD=1 prefix is only needed for hybrid GPU laptops (Optimus systems).

Current Known Issue

The volumetric visualizer currently has a render-space transformation issue causing flow structures to visually drift downward.

The underlying simulation data and numerical results remain correct.

Disclaimer
Experimental research/learning project — not validated for safety-critical engineering use.
